fc84b6d36c5b","taskId":"instruments"},{"mergeCommit":"b474021c40d16a6bd0fce9ac2b9002b4e6538cc4","pullRequest":"local://mecattaf/flashnext/tally/flashnext-campaign-01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae/host-tooling-ab66c582012f053f","revision":"sha256:ab66c582012f053ffa092301faf6a9b042d52ad26c6baa1b6d149083241af99d","taskId":"host-tooling"},{"mergeCommit":"71f2beba0ecd7358eda99e574e078d081f55bbfa","pullRequest":"local://mecattaf/flashnext/tally/flashnext-campaign-01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae/bench-harness-3a8882e61c9b2ce9","revision":"sha256:3a8882e61c9b2ce9ef7a7904e06778f0284df952e4a68deb4f8e6e1caba1a225","taskId":"bench-harness"}],"checkpoints":[],"remaining":["proxy-tooling","morning-ledger","catalog-handoff","rdma-package","cp-weights","cp-build","cp-smoke","cp-proxy","cp-tp2","cp-bench","cp-close"],"frontier":["proxy-tooling"],"diagnoses":[{"attempt":1,"comment":"local://campaign/flashnext/attempt-receipts/15","diagnosis":"Aborted in the lane stage before any worktree was prepared, so no worker ever ran and no task content was implicated. The recorded failure is a flow-error whose detail is the harness exception FlowAdmissionDenied (code admission-denied, ordinal 4, at line 3377 column 25) with an empty details object; exitCode is null and captureStderr is empty, meaning no command was executed and no gate ran. gateOutputs is empty, workerOutcomeClaim is null, previousWorkerOutcomes and previousDiagnoses are empty, and the diff is unavailable with reason 'task failed before a worktree was prepared' at base rev all-zeros. Nothing in the task morning-ledger points at the failure: the sole acceptance criterion ledger-sections is a plain grep over docs/MORNING.md and docs/ANNOUNCE.md, both inside the authorized docs conflict domain, and it was never evaluated. The dependencies host-tooling and bench-harness are also not implicated, because dependency resolution would surface as a task-level block rather than an admission denial raised inside the flow engine itself. Admission denial at lane entry with no stderr, no exit code, and no worktree is a scheduler/session fault in the machinery that admits lanes, not an authorable defect in the repository and not a gate-contract or authority problem the operator must grant. The correct disposition is therefore to charge the bounded machinery-retry budget and re-admit the lane unchanged; if admission is denied again at the same ordinal, the fault is durable in the flow layer and should be escalated to the operator rather than retried further.","taskId":"morning-ledger","verdict":"blocked"},{"attempt":1,"comment":"local://campaign/flashnext/attempt-receipts/18","diagnosis":"Failed at lane admission before any worktree, worker invocation, or gate execution occurred, so no task-content defect is implicated. Evidence: the failure stage is `lane` with verdict `flow-error` and detail `FlowAdmissionDenied` / code `admission-denied` (ordinal 4, empty details), exitCode is null and captureStderr is empty, gateOutputs is empty, workerOutcomeClaim is null, previousWorkerOutcomes and previousDiagnoses are empty, and the diff is unavailable with reason \"task failed before a worktree was prepared\". Because the flow controller refused to admit the lane, the worker never read specs/flashnext/spec.md#r5 and never created handoff/catalog-row.patch or handoff/README.md; the sole acceptance criterion catalog-patch-wellformed was never evaluated, and there is no failing check id or offending path to cite. Nothing in the task is at fault: it is an implementation task with no dependencies, a single conflict domain of \"handoff\" that is also its only authorized write prefix, and no needs-authority envelope was returned. There is likewise no out-of-task cause to name — no missing authority, no gate-contract defect, no upstream source fix, since the denial carries no adjudicable reason payload and no work product exists to attribute it to. This is a scheduler/session-level admission fault in the campaign machinery (for example lane-slot or conflict-domain admission contention on \"handoff\"), which is precisely what the bounded machinery-retry budget covers; a re-admission of the identical lane at revision sha256:3a04f0fc89c3e88303af3a5b38fc8a4bd52f2f81715bfecfc42bdc04ba5c2269 is the correct next action. If admission is denied again with the same code and still-empty details, the recurrence stops being incidental and should be escalated to the operator as a flow-configuration problem rather than continuing to consume retries.","taskId":"catalog-handoff","verdict":"blocked"},{"attempt":1,"comment":"local://campaign/flashnext/attempt-receipts/21","diagnosis":"Failed during lane admission before any worktree, worker, or gate execution occurred, so nothing about the task's content was exercised. The failure record carries stage \"lane\", verdict \"flow-error\", a null exit code, empty stderr, and detail {\"name\":\"FlowAdmissionDenied\",\"code\":\"admission-denied\",\"line\":3377,\"column\":25,\"ordinal\":4,\"details\":{}} with no populated details payload. Corroborating evidence: gateOutputs is empty, workerOutcomeClaim is null, previousWorkerOutcomes is empty, and the diff block reports available=false with reason \"task failed before a worktree was prepared\" and a null head against the all-zero base revision. There is therefore no failing check id and no offending path to cite, because no acceptance criterion ran; the sole criterion rdma-package-sound was never invoked. The task definition itself shows no admission-blocking defect: it declares no dependencies, its conflictDomains [\"host/rdma\",\"tests\"] cover every path its goal directs it to write (host/rdma/fetch-and-build.sh, host/rdma/attended-bringup.md, host/rdma/ab-protocol.md, and the tests suite extension), and its read-only references to specs/flashnext/spec.md#r6, specs/flashnext/evidence/ds4-vllm-manifest.md, specs/flashnext/evidence/nix-hardening-addendum.md, and scripts/stage-weights.sh require no write authority outside those domains. The worker envelope did not request authority, so the always-blocked needs-authority path does not apply. That leaves an orchestration-side admission refusal — the flow machinery declining to open the lane at ordinal 4 — rather than an actionable in-task fix or an out-of-task authority, dependency, or gate-contract defect. Re-dispatch of the identical task revision sha256:b322b54d6da9831c25a2e55569a9a8ce4c293840285b6225b2760d2c20ee9460 against a healthy lane is the correct next action; it should consume the bounded machinery-retry budget and not the task's two-attempt cap. If admission is denied again with the same code and an empty details payload, escalate to the operator as a flow-layer fault rather than re-diagnosing the task, since no repository change under host/rdma or tests could alter this outcome.","taskId":"rdma-package","verdict":"blocked"}],"retries":[{"attempt":1,"comment":"local://campaign/flashnext/attempt-receipts/23","reason":"Stage `lane` faulted.\n\n{\"name\":\"FlowAdmissionDenied\",\"code\":\"admission-denied\",\"line\":3377,\"column\":25,\"ordinal\":4,\"details\":{}}","taskId":"proxy-tooling"},{"attempt":1,"comment":"local://campaign/flashnext/attempt-receipts/13","reason":"Stage `lane` faulted.\n\n{\"name\":\"FlowAdmissionDenied\",\"code\":\"admission-denied\",\"line\":3377,\"column\":25,\"ordinal\":4,\"details\":{}}","taskId":"morning-ledger"},{"attempt":2,"comment":"local://campaign/flashnext/attempt-receipts/14","reason":"Stage `lane` faulted.\n\n{\"name\":\"FlowAdmissionDenied\",\"code\":\"admission-denied\",\"line\":3377,\"column\":25,\"ordinal\":4,\"details\":{}}","taskId":"morning-ledger"},{"attempt":1,"comment":"local://campaign/flashnext/attempt-receipts/16","reason":"Stage `lane` faulted.\n\n{\"name\":\"FlowAdmissionDenied\",\"code\":\"admission-denied\",\"line\":3377,\"column\":25,\"ordinal\":4,\"details\":{}}","taskId":"catalog-handoff"},{"attempt":2,"comment":"local://campaign/flashnext/atte